From: TunaOS packagers <packages@tunaos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Include the libxfce4panel umbrella header

Upstream: https://gitlab.xfce.org/panel-plugins/xfce4-datetime-plugin
Upstream-Status: Pending (not submitted yet; master at 78c89324 still has
 the direct include, and the last release, 0.8.3, is from 2023)
Reason: datetime-dialog.c includes libxfce4panel/xfce-panel-plugin.h
 directly. Since xfce4-panel 4.21 the sub-headers error out unless they
 come through libxfce4panel/libxfce4panel.h, so the plugin does not build
 against the 4.21 series. The other panel plugins made the same change in
 their 2025 releases.

--- a/panel-plugin/datetime-dialog.c
+++ b/panel-plugin/datetime-dialog.c
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 /* xfce includes */
 #include <libxfce4ui/libxfce4ui.h>
 #include <libxfce4util/libxfce4util.h>
-#include <libxfce4panel/xfce-panel-plugin.h>
+#include <libxfce4panel/libxfce4panel.h>
 
 #include "datetime.h"
 #include "datetime-dialog.h"
